# Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io), seeded by
# swarm-routing/.github org-sync (`citation = true`; `citation_type` and
# `[[references]]` in .github/org-sync.toml); the repository's own once
# written. Commitizen keeps `version:` in step (`.cz.toml` version_files
# "CITATION.cff:^version:"); swarm-routing/.github tools/zenodo reads the
# concept DOI from `doi:` once the first release is archived on Zenodo.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "swarm-adapter-omnet: the OMNeT++/INET adapter of swarm-core"
abstract: >-
  swarm-adapter-omnet, the OMNeT++/INET adapter of swarm-core's ports
  (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24476619): the OMNeT++ module a
  swarm-routing protocol's simulator-free core runs on inside OMNeT++/INET,
  as swarm-adapter-ns3 is for ns-3. It converts and carries out a core's
  decisions (clock, randomness, timers, neighbours, link state, deferred
  packets) and holds no routing logic.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Joppi
    given-names: Daniel Henrique
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6436-8174"
version: "0.0.0"
license: GPL-2.0-only
